{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations\/destination"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Destinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships"},{"title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination"],"type":"conformingTypes","kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each destination its batches in the order the events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"were tracked, one at a time: the next batch comes once "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns. Batches that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops its oldest batch when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full, so a destination that falls behind doesn’t hold up the others."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The delivery reports each batch dropped. Once the destination has caught up, it gets the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dropped batch’s records that a store keeps, read back from the store, after the newer batches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it received meanwhile; those kept in memory only are lost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" should return as soon as the batch is somewhere it won’t be lost, and honour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancellation: a delivery waits for it before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancelled. Until it returns, this destination’s later batches wait in its buffer. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination handles its own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When a tracker keeps its records in a store, returning from ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)"},{"text":" is what tells the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store a batch arrived: once every destination has returned for it, uncancelled, the store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"forgets those records. A destination that buffers or retries should return only once the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch is somewhere it won’t be lost; a record whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered"},{"text":" is set may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have reached it in an earlier run.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers rather than by code of its own:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()"},{"type":"text","text":". A destination given none receives every record as tracked."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Destinations"}],"externalID":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol","title":"Destination","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Destination.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Destinations\/Destination.swift#L27"},"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"identifier"}]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/enriched(by:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Destinations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","doc:\/\/Desti